# AWS Secrets Manager User Guide

> Walks you through creating and managing your secrets, retrieving them in your application, and automatically rotating them to help keep them secure.

- [What is Secrets Manager?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.md)
- [Access Secrets Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/asm_access.md)
- [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/best-practices.md)
- [API keys for sensitive workloads](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/api-keys-security-sensitive.md)
- [AWS CDK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/cdk.md)
- [Compliance validation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/secretsmanager-compliance.md)
- [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/troubleshoot.md)
- [Quotas](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/reference_limits.md)
- [Document history](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/document-history.md)

## [Tutorials](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/tutorials.md)

- [Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/integrating-codeguru.md): Learn how to use CodeGuru Reviewer to find unprotected secrets in your Java and Python code.
- [Replace hardcoded secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/hardcoded.md): Replace hardcoded secrets in your code with AWS Secrets Manager secrets.
- [Replace hardcoded DB credentials](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/hardcoded-db-creds.md): Learn how to replace hardcoded credentials with AWS Secrets Manager secrets.
- [Alternating users rotation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/tutorials_rotation-alternating.md): Learn how to set up automatic rotation for database credentials.
- [Single user rotation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/tutorials_rotation-single.md): Learn how to set up automatic rotation for database credentials.


## [Create secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/create_secret.md)

- [What's in a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/whats-in-a-secret.md): Describes the components of a Secrets Manager secret.
- [JSON structure of a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/reference_secret_json_structure.md): Learn what to store in a secret.


## [Manage secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/managing-secrets.md)

- [Update a secret value](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_update-secret-value.md): Learn how to update AWS Secrets Manager secrets.
- [Generate a password with Secrets Manager](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/generate-password.md): A common pattern for using Secrets Manager is to generate a password in Secrets Manager and then use that password in your database or service.
- [Roll back a secret to a previous version](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/roll-back-secret.md): Learn how to roll back an AWS Secrets Manager secret to a previous version.
- [Change the encryption key for a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_update-encryption-key.md): Learn how to change the encryption key for an AWS Secrets Manager secret.
- [Modify a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_update-secret.md): Learn how you can update a secret.
- [Find secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_search-secret.md): Learn how to find secrets using a variety of filters, including name and the service that manages the secret.
- [Delete a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_delete-secret.md): Learn how to delete a secret.
- [Restore a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/manage_restore-secret.md): In Secrets Manager, restore a secret that was scheduled to be deleted.
- [Tag secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/managing-secrets_tagging.md): Learn how to use tags to organize and manage your secrets in AWS Secrets Manager.


## [Multi-region replication](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/replicate-secrets.md)

- [Promote a replica secret to a standalone secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/standalone-secret.md): Learn how to promote a replica secret to a standalone secret.
- [Prevent replication](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/replicate-secrets-permissions.md): Learn how to prevent users from replicating secrets to other Regions in AWS Secrets Manager.
- [Troubleshoot replication](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/replicate-secrets_troubleshoot.md): Troubleshoot issues with AWS Secrets Manager secret replication.


## [Get secrets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets.md)

### [Java](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-java.md)

In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [Java with client-side caching](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-java.md)

In Secrets Manager, retrieve secrets in Java applications.

- [SecretCache](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-java-ref_SecretCache.md): An in-memory cache for secrets requested from Secrets Manager.
- [SecretCacheConfiguration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-java-ref_SecretCacheConfiguration.md): Cache configuration options for a , such as max cache size and Time to Live (TTL) for cached secrets.
- [SecretCacheHook](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-java-ref_SecretCacheHook.md): An interface to hook into a to perform actions on the secrets being stored in the cache.
- [JDBC connection with credentials in a secret](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_jdbc.md): Use JDBC to connect to a database using credentials stored in a secret.
- [Java AWS SDK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-java-sdk.md): In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [Python](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-python.md)

In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [Python with client-side caching](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-python.md)

In Secrets Manager, retrieve secrets in Python applications.

- [SecretCache](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-ref-secretcache.md): An in-memory cache for secrets retrieved from Secrets Manager.
- [SecretCacheConfig](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-ref-secretcacheconfig.md): Cache configuration options for a such as max cache size and Time to Live (TTL) for cached secrets.
- [SecretCacheHook](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-ref-secretcachehook.md): An interface to hook into a to perform actions on the secrets being stored in the cache.
- [@InjectSecretString](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-decor-string.md): This decorator expects a secret ID string and as the first and second arguments.
- [@InjectKeywordedSecretString](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-decor-keyword.md): This decorator expects a secret ID string and as the first and second arguments.
- [Python AWS SDK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-python-sdk.md): In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.
- [Get a batch of secret values](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-python-batch.md): The following code example shows how to get a batch of Secrets Manager secret values.

### [.NET](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-net.md)

In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [.NET with client-side caching](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-net.md)

Learn how to retrieve secrets in .NET applications.

- [SecretsManagerCache](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-net-SecretsManagerCache.md): An in-memory cache for secrets requested from Secrets Manager.
- [SecretCacheConfiguration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-net-SecretCacheConfiguration.md): Cache configuration options for a , such as maximum cache size and Time to Live (TTL) for cached secrets.
- [ISecretCacheHook](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-net-ISecretCacheHook.md): An interface to hook into a to perform actions on the secrets being stored in the cache.
- [SDK for .NET](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-net-sdk.md): In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [Go](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-go.md)

In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

### [Go with client-side caching](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-go.md)

In Secrets Manager, retrieve secrets in Go applications.

- [type Cache](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-go_cache.md): An in-memory cache for secrets requested from Secrets Manager.
- [type CacheConfig](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-go_CacheConfig.md): Cache configuration options for a Cache, such as maximum cache size, default version stage, and Time to Live (TTL) for cached secrets.
- [type CacheHook](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets_cache-go_CacheHook.md): An interface to hook into a Cache to perform actions on the secret being stored in the cache.
- [Go AWS SDK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/retrieving-secrets-go-sdk.md): In applications, you can retrieve your secrets by calling GetSecretValue or BatchGetSecretValuein any of the AWS SDKs.

